USOS CSMWrap patch 0016 (2026-10-18): USB mouse wheel (IntelliMouse emulation)

SeaBIOS serves a USB mouse as the BIOS PS/2 pointing device (INT 15h
C2xxh) in the HID boot protocol: 3-byte packets, no wheel. With this patch:
- usb_mouse_setup reads the interface's HID report descriptor (GET_DESCRIPTOR
  0x22, buffer zeroed first) and walks it minimally (buttons 1-3, relative
  X/Y, relative wheel 0x01:0x38 of the report that has X; report IDs; fields
  up to 16 bits; one Push level). With a wheel found, and every input report
  of the interface no longer than one interrupt packet, it switches the
  mouse to the report protocol and decodes that layout; packets of other
  report IDs (consumer, keyboard macro reports of gaming mice) are ignored.
  Otherwise (no wheel, nested Push, long items, a longer report, any error)
  it stays in the boot protocol exactly as before. SET_PROTOCOL is per
  interface; SeaBIOS uses only the first boot HID interface of a device,
  keyboards stay in the boot protocol unchanged.
- PS/2 IntelliMouse emulation: sample rates 200, 100, 80 (INT 15h C202h)
  switch the device ID to 3 (only when a wheel mouse is present); C204h
  returns the device ID (was 0AAh, the BAT code, for USB mice); C201h /
  C205h reset it to 0.
- C205h accepts package sizes 1..7 (was 3 only). Package size 3: three bytes
  as before; after the knock the wheel byte (IntelliMouse sign: up is
  negative) is passed in the handler's Z word (always 0 before). Package
  size 4..7: status, X, Y, wheel (0 without the knock), zero padding; the
  handler's Z word is the 4th byte. Package size 1/2: a byte stream of 3
  bytes, 4 after the knock (VBADOS VBMOUSE "streaming" mode).
- USB mice with wMaxPacketSize 9..16 are accepted (were refused).
Clients that never send the knock see the old behaviour (3-byte packets,
Z = 0). Consumers: USOSKEY.COM/USOSKEY.DRV ring + USOSMOUS.DRV (Windows
98/98 SE/Me WM_MOUSEWHEEL), VBADOS VBMOUSE.EXE 0.67 unmodified (INT 33h
wheel API in DOS).

Own code (HID 1.11 report descriptor format, IBM PS/2 BIOS C2xxh and the
public IntelliMouse PS/2 knock). Applies after 0001-0010, 0012, 0014, 0015
(no common file), patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of a MODIFIED
CSMWrap made by the USOS project (SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

